media: h713-hdmirx: an unlisted raster is caught where it really ends - the INCAP sanity check

1600x900 still read "change in flight" for ever on dev21, with 0136m, 0136r
and 0136u in place. An instrumented driver (every -ENOLCK return numbered)
showed which one answers: the INCAP sanity check "no geometry". For a raster
its table does not carry the firmware writes its record (1600x900, signal_id
1, 60.00 Hz) and the new TOTALS into INCAP (1800x1000), but leaves INCAP's
ACTIVE word at the mode before (1920x1080) and the capture off. The totals
then read smaller than the active size, the check takes that for "no
geometry" and returns -ENOLCK on every poll - before the record, the
stale-record test or the pre-check of 0136r/0136u are reached at all.

So the record is consulted right there: when the totals are present, the
record is genuine and its raster is in no table record (geometry only, the
0136u rule), the answer is unlisted, with the record's raster and rate in the
timing the ioctl hands back and one journal line per state. Everything else
about that check stays as it was (the TVFE/TVCAP power-domain case reads all
zeros and still gets its line and -ENOLCK).

Measured on the HY310 (dev21 debug kernel, module swapped over the LAN):
1600x900 -> "source 1600x900 at 60.00 Hz: in none of the firmware's mode
records -- no lock" exactly once, h713-tv "not in the firmware's table --
console"; 1024x768 after 1366x768 still locks (record lag, raster in the
table); 1080p60 locks; no line at any 50/24 Hz mode. Open: h713-tv prints
"0x0p?, 0.0 MHz" for the refused source although the timing is filled here -
its capture_signal() keeps the timing only on success.

Amended 22.09. night (dev22): the blanking is filled as well, so h713-tv shows
1600x900p60 and not p75 (it computes the rate over the totals).

Follow-up to 0136m/0136r/0136u (review Q9, device run 22.09.2026 afternoon).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

--- a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c
@@ -3682,6 +3682,35 @@
 	htotal = total & 0xffff;
 	if (!width || !height || htotal <= width || vtotal <= height) {
 		/*
+		 * A raster the firmware's table does not carry ends here, for
+		 * ever: the firmware writes its record (1600x900, signal_id 1)
+		 * and the new totals into INCAP (1800x1000), but leaves the
+		 * ACTIVE word at the mode before (1920x1080) and the capture
+		 * off - so the totals read smaller than the active size and
+		 * this check answered "change in flight" on every poll (dev21,
+		 * 22.09.2026, instrumented). The record can say what INCAP
+		 * cannot: a record raster in no table record is unlisted.
+		 */
+		if (htotal && vtotal && have_sig && !own_record &&
+		    rx->tse_count && sig.h_size && sig.v_size &&
+		    !h713_hdmirx_tse_carries(rx, sig.h_size, sig.v_size,
+					     htotal, vtotal)) {
+			/* the measurement travels with the error (0136m) */
+			memset(t, 0, sizeof(*t));
+			t->type = V4L2_DV_BT_656_1120;
+			t->bt.width = sig.h_size;
+			t->bt.height = sig.v_size;
+			t->bt.pixelclock = div_u64((u64)htotal * vtotal *
+						   sig.frame_rate_x100, 100);
+			/* the totals too, or a client computes the rate over the active size */
+			t->bt.hbackporch = htotal - sig.h_size;
+			t->bt.vbackporch = vtotal - sig.v_size;
+			return h713_hdmirx_unlisted(rx,
+					(sig.h_size << 16) | sig.v_size,
+					sig.frame_rate_x100,
+					"in none of the firmware's mode records");
+		}
+		/*
 		 * The whole block reads zero while the TVFE/TVCAP power
 		 * domain is off (doku/78 section 0). No capture runs in that
 		 * state either, so this deserves a line, not silence.
